  "dialog.unsafeEmphasisDetails": "CommonMark does not only check whether asterisks are paired. It also checks the characters on both sides of each marker. When the inside of the marker touches punctuation and the outside touches Chinese, English, or a number, the marker is usually not treated as bold or italic. It usually works when the outside is whitespace, punctuation, or the start/end of a line. Converting to HTML preserves the visual formatting and prevents literal asterisks from appearing the next time the document is opened."
